invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: crt_combine returns without wiping h, Garner's factor qinv * (m1
  - m2) mod p, which with the signature and q's multiple of it gives a
  prime. Inside a signature a later call's frame is written over that
  one, so bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test calls the recombination on its own
  (test/rsa_sign_equiv_pieces.c), copies the stack below it and finds two
  limbs of the value there.

--- old
    ct_wipe(t, sizeof t);
    ct_wipe(h, sizeof h);
--- new
    ct_wipe(t, sizeof t);
